TASK (exactly one change): cli-opencode now has a per-version default model, and the docs already say so: OpenCode 1 uses `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (`--model ... --variant max`), OpenCode 2 uses `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (`-m ...#max`). In `references/providers-and-models.md` the `### opencode-go` table marks the v1 default with `✓` and the `### llmgateway` table marks the v2 default with `✓`.

Update `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/scripts/tests/default-model-id.test.cjs` to hold the tree to that:
1. Rename `DEFAULT_ID` to `V1_DEFAULT_ID` and add `V2_DEFAULT_ID = 'llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash'`, each with a one-line comment on where it is listed.
2. Keep 'the roster names one opencode-go default' (now against `V1_DEFAULT_ID`) and add the same test for the `llmgateway` table and `V2_DEFAULT_ID`.
3. In "SKILL.md's default invocation names the roster default", require every `--model` selector to pin `V1_DEFAULT_ID` and every `-m` selector to pin `V2_DEFAULT_ID` (still requiring at least one of each). Rename the test to say it names each version's roster default.
4. Add one test that the two defaults differ in exactly one way: the same model slug after the provider, and the providers `opencode-go` and `llmgateway`.
5. Update the header comment so it describes the per-version default. Leave the retired-id test unchanged.

